0..70 Comment "// The manifold that deploys the migration model across two processes."
71..73 Comment "//"
74..151 Comment "// A manifold binds a program\'s worlds onto sites, so one program runs as two"
152..201 Comment "// processes without naming either in its source."
202..204 Comment "//"
205..278 Comment "// This one deploys the migration model beside it and places `far` at the"
279..356 Comment "// site it imports, reading its key and socket there. `near`, where the entry"
357..431 Comment "// runs, is placed nowhere: it is the process that runs `main`. `gandr run"
432..489 Comment "// --manifold` and `gandr host --manifold` read it as the"
490..538 Comment "// `--world far=<key>@<ip:port>` it desugars to."
539..541 Comment "//"
542..605 Comment "// - see: `two-processes.site.gandr` — the site `far` runs at"
606..664 Comment "// - see: `two-processes.gandr` — the program it deploys"
665..733 Comment "// - see: `crates/surface-driver/tests/net.rs` — the two processes"
735..795 Comment "// The deployment theories, from `std.manifold` by its path."
